# 6. HUMAN REVIEW PROGRESS AND "ĐẠT BAO NHIÊU"

The customer specifically wants to see how many criteria an application has met.

Implement an accurate, easy-to-understand presentation.

For Individual Student 5-Good applications:

- Đạo đức tốt.
- Học tập tốt.
- Thể lực tốt.
- Tình nguyện tốt.
- Hội nhập tốt.

At the appropriate human review level, calculate:

- Number of criteria with completed review.
- Number assessed as meeting requirements.
- Number assessed as not meeting requirements.
- Number not yet completely reviewed.
- Number awaiting supplementation, where applicable.

Use existing canonical aggregation logic.

If a criterion has unresolved mandatory requirement judgments, do not simply count it as completed.

Preserve actual ONE_OF and ALL_OF criteria semantics.

### Important distinctions

**5/5 tiêu chí đạt** is an assessed criteria result.

It is NOT automatically a Committee recognition decision.

An application partially reviewed but currently meeting 3 criteria must not be falsely classified as a fully assessed "Đạt 3/5" dossier.

Use clear labels or filters to distinguish:

- Review in progress.
- Fully reviewed.
- Number of criteria meeting requirements.
- Final official recognition result.

No AI preliminary outcome may contribute to official human review counters.

