# 13. MODERN ANALYTICS AND CHARTS

Create a polished reporting experience.

Choose useful chart types such as:

- Bar chart: applications by institution.
- Stacked bar chart: workflow status by institution.
- Donut chart: major status breakdown.
- Bar chart: number of human-assessed criteria meeting requirements.
- Trend chart: submissions over time, only where meaningful timestamp data exists.

Do not add charts merely to fill the page.

Each chart must have:

- Clear title.
- Explicit metric definition.
- Appropriate denominator.
- Relevant filters.
- Accessible labels.
- Consistent data source.
- Responsive behavior.
- Empty/loading/error states.

### Critical counting rules

Document exactly:

- Which application types are included.
- Which award season is selected.
- Which review scope is used.
- Which application statuses are included.
- Whether a metric is based on submitted, reviewed, recommended or officially recognized records.
- How cancelled, archived, duplicate and draft records are treated.

Use one authoritative aggregation contract.

Do not calculate a dashboard KPI one way and the corresponding exported report another way.

