# 14. EXCEL EXPORT — REAL FUNCTIONALITY

The customer values the legacy system's Excel export functions.

Implement or improve authorized Excel exports.

### Recommended exports

- Individual application list.
- School recommended application list.
- School consolidated forwarding list.
- City review progress list.
- Committee results list.
- Collective application list.
- Authorized aggregated statistical report.

Only expose exports actually supported by the implemented business model and permissions.

### Export behavior

- Respect award season.
- Respect role and resource scope.
- Respect active filters.
- Include clear column headings.
- Include original institution.
- Preserve leading zeros in identifier fields.
- Format dates correctly.
- Represent missing values honestly.
- Distinguish human review results from AI advisory results.
- Include official decisions only when actually recorded.

Generate an actual downloadable `.xlsx` file when exporting Excel.

Do not implement a decorative Download button.

Do not merely rename CSV to `.xlsx`.

Use an existing suitable backend/frontend export library if present.

Do not add unnecessary heavy dependencies.

### Export security

Apply resource-level authorization server-side for Real Mode.

Do not let a client export data outside its scope by modifying query parameters.

Prevent spreadsheet formula injection in user-controlled text values.

Protect personal data.

Avoid exporting unnecessary sensitive fields by default.

Do not expose private evidence file URLs.

If bulk exports may be large, use an appropriate efficient existing backend export pattern rather than downloading the entire dataset into the browser.

